= July 2025 — A meeting is evidence, not a verdict

After demanding a coalition renegotiation, Sejm Marshal and Poland 2050 founder
<span class="party-p2050"><b>Szymon Hołownia</b></span> meets **Adam Bielan**, a PiS-aligned MEP and experienced
right-wing negotiator. PiS chair <span class="party-pis"><b>Jarosław Kaczyński</b></span> also attends. Public
reporting establishes who entered the room, not whether they discussed ordinary
dialogue, a bargaining bluff or the votes for another majority.

[? if third_way_active: Third Way survived June. PSL can demand that talks
affecting its common electoral brand pass through a joint council. PSL leader
<span class="party-psl"><b>Władysław Kosiniak-Kamysz</b></span> must decide whether party autonomy includes a
partner privately testing the right.?]
[? if third_way_split: Third Way has already divided. PSL and Poland 2050 now
answer for their own channels, while the coalition must test Hołownia's claims
against actual Sejm arithmetic.?]

For Lewica, outrage is easy and proof is harder. If we govern together, an
unfounded accusation can break the majority we claim to protect; if we sit in
opposition, a realignment could change the government before the public sees a
single written term. We must decide what evidence earns trust and what conduct
ends it.

- @night_joint_audit
- @night_party_autonomy
- @night_joint_accuse
- @night_minutes
- @night_open_channels
- @night_split_accuse

@night_joint_audit
title: Put all cross-party talks before a joint Third Way council
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Keep both parties free to talk, but make them share minutes and arithmetic.
view-if: third_way_active = 1
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The parliamentary audit cannot be staffed.
on-arrival: {! Q.resources -= 1; Q.third_way_night_meeting_response = "Joint minutes and arithmetic audit"; Q.third_way_cohesion = Math.min(100, (Number(Q.third_way_cohesion) || 0) + 8); Q.p2050_coalition_dissent -= 2; Q.psl_coalition_dissent -= 2; Q.rival_relation_psl_p2050 += 4; Q.public_trust += 2; Q.news_headline = "Third Way answers the night meeting with shared minutes and a seat count"; !}

Hołownia and Kosiniak-Kamysz submit future cross-party contacts to a joint
council with minutes and a live seat count. Neither party surrenders the right
to talk; both surrender the right to tell their common voters incompatible
stories about what the talk could produce.

- @poland_event_queue: File the joint Third Way audit

@night_party_autonomy
title: Accept separate contacts while preserving the common list
subtitle: Respect each party's autonomy and leave common-list voters with two possible coalition stories.
view-if: third_way_active = 1
on-arrival: third_way_night_meeting_response = "Separate party channels under the common list"; p2050_relation += 2; psl_relation += 2; p2050_coalition_dissent -= 1; third_way_cohesion -= 4; public_trust -= 1; news_headline = "Third Way survives by separating its electoral pact from coalition diplomacy"

Lewica accepts that Poland 2050 and PSL may hold separate talks while their
electoral pact survives. Relations with both leaderships improve because we do
not demand custody of their diaries. Third Way's voters are left to wonder what
a common list means when its parties can negotiate different governments.

- @poland_event_queue: Record separate channels under one list

@night_joint_accuse
title: Denounce the meeting as preparation for a new majority
subtitle: Unite Lewica around a clear charge before there is a named partner or a seat count.
